# Coding practices

## Backend (Python)

- Ruff for lint + format; MyPy in strict mode on `src/soulwalker`.
- Type every public function. Prefer explicit errors (`ValueError`, domain exceptions) over returning `None` for failures.
- Small modules. One domain concern per service. No god-services, no logic in FastAPI routers.
- Pydantic schemas at the API boundary; SQLAlchemy models stay in `models/`.
- Config via environment variables (`pydantic-settings`). Never commit secrets.

## Flutter

- Strict `analysis_options.yaml`. `prefer_const_constructors`, avoid `dynamic`, avoid `print`.
- Functional widgets; extract logic into domain classes / notifiers. No business rules in `build()`.
- Use `TermKey` / `TerminologyResolver` for mythos strings. Engine identifiers stay generic.

## Shared

- Names: `snake_case` Python, `camelCase` Dart members, `PascalCase` types.
- Do not catch-and-swallow. Log with context, then re-raise or map to an HTTP/UI error.
- Keep diffs focused. Do not add comments that only narrate what the code already says.
